This appears to be a CBP ruling on an electrochemical water purification system. Heading 8421 covers filtering or purifying machinery for liquids. Subheading 8421.21 covers water filtering or purifying machinery and apparatus, and its statistical suffixes are 8421.21.0000 (the 10-digit form is 8421.21.0000). Since the system is housed in a container, it could be argued that it is a composite machine or a functional unit, but its principal function is water purification, so 8421.21 is the best fit. Electrolytic apparatus under 8543.30 is a possible alternative, but electrolysis there refers to electroplating, electrolysis and electrophoresis machines. The system's purpose is water purification, so 8421 is more specific.

HTS 8421.21.00 has the statistical suffixes 8421.21.0010 (reverse osmosis and similar types), 8421.21.0090 (other) and others, though I'm not certain of the exact breakdown. I believe the current structure is 8421.21.00 with 10-digit codes 8421.21.0000 for "Water filtering or purifying machinery and apparatus". I'll go with 8421.21.0000.

{"hts_code": "8421.21.0000", "reason": "The system is machinery for purifying water (heading 8421, subheading 8421.21), which is its principal function as a functional unit, even though it is housed in a modified container."}
